### Inventory Service - try it with the REST Client extension (click "Send Request" above each block)
### Start infra first:  cd infra; docker compose up -d --wait
### Start the service:  .\mvnw.cmd -pl inventory-service -am spring-boot:run
### The seeder gives SKU-00001 ... SKU-01000 a stock level of 0..50 (same SKUs as product-service).

@base = http://localhost:8082/api/inventory

### 1. Stock for several SKUs in one call (order-service will use this to check a cart)
GET {{base}}?skus=SKU-00001,SKU-00002,SKU-00003

### 2. Restock (upsert): set the available quantity
PUT {{base}}/SKU-00001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "available": 20 }

### 3. Reserve stock for an order - all or nothing. 201 Created the first time...
POST {{base}}/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "DEMO-ORDER-1",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "SKU-00001", "quantity": 2 },
    { "sku": "SKU-00002", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### 4. ...send request 3 again: 200 OK, same reservation, stock NOT reserved twice (idempotency)

### 5. Stock moved from "available" to "reserved"
GET {{base}}?skus=SKU-00001,SKU-00002

### 6. Look up the reservation
GET {{base}}/reservations/DEMO-ORDER-1

### 7. Payment failed -> release (saga compensation). Send it twice: the second call changes nothing.
POST {{base}}/reservations/DEMO-ORDER-1/release

### 8. Confirm after release -> 409 (invalid state)
POST {{base}}/reservations/DEMO-ORDER-1/confirm

### 9. All or nothing: SKU-00001 has enough, but 999 of SKU-00002 doesn't -> 409, NOTHING is reserved
POST {{base}}/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "DEMO-ORDER-2",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "SKU-00001", "quantity": 1 },
    { "sku": "SKU-00002", "quantity": 999 }
  ]
}

### 10. Confirm path: reserve, then confirm (payment succeeded) -> reserved stock becomes sold
POST {{base}}/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "DEMO-ORDER-3", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-00003", "quantity": 1 } ] }

###
POST {{base}}/reservations/DEMO-ORDER-3/confirm

### 11. Validation error -> 400 with one violation per field
POST {{base}}/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-00001", "quantity": 0 } ] }

### 12. Retry metric (non-zero only after concurrent conflicts)
GET http://localhost:8082/actuator/metrics/inventory.reservation.retries
